    },
    {
      "key": "settings.media.maxActive.tooltip",
      "value": "How many media players may play at once. The furthest ones stop and start again when you go back to them. 0 removes the limit, which on a headset will cost you bandwidth and frame rate."
    },
    {
      "key": "settings.media.bufferDepth",
      "value": "Default buffer depth (ms)"
    },
    {
      "key": "settings.media.bufferDepth.tooltip",
      "value": "How much media is held back before playing, to ride out a patchy connection. Applies to every media player you have not tuned individually from the Media Players panel. 0 is Auto, which works it out from the connection and is the right answer for almost everyone. Raising it makes playback steadier and slower to start."
    },
